&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You run your own day. You manage your own work, unblock yourself where you can, and shout early and clearly when you can&#39;t.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build to last. Resilient, maintainable, observable. You hold a high bar on testing and code review - and you&#39;ll be surrounded by people who hold it too, which is the fastest way to raise your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You share the load. That includes pitching in on operational work and an on-call rotation for critical alerts - because the people who built the systems are the people best placed to keep them healthy. We take on-call seriously and it’s our job to not make it miserable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You get better, and you help others get better. We rotate on solution ownership,&amp;nbsp; we collaborate within and across teams, we take part in engineering Guild sessions, we write RFCs, we mentor where it’s welcomed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll know what &quot;next&quot; looks like. We have a progression framework and growth is a conversation, not a guessing game.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
